On Thu, 19 Jan 2006, Christopher Calzonetti wrote:
>
> Lemurs aside, when one knocks down everything around the door, why is it
> that diagonals still don't work, but BOTH orthogonal directions work?
> If the door is an East-West facing door, shouldn't walking into the
> square from the North or South mean that you're walking smack into the
> side of the door frame?

   Doors in the dungeon are square (obviously, as they take up a square 
patch on the screen). They consist of four posts, one in each corner of
the square, with a revolving door in the middle. The revolving door can
be locked against turning. Digging down in the middle of the four posts
causes the doorframe to fall into the pit and break up.
   You can't walk diagonally into a door square because one of the posts
is in the way.

